#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082971 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8922ab07-5ac7-5f85-bfee-c30de7f4024a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Parametric Curve"}] :question/id #uuid "15c029df-b002-51cc-87db-a94d40a02771" :question/math-academy-id "e-595" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n$x=\\cos{t}, \\quad y=\\sin{t}, \\qquad 0\\leq t<2\\pi$, calculate $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/798/Source/Images/0f8bfc82b98e63e586e9d2e96d1acc5d.png)" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y$, we get\n\n$$\nx'(t) = -\\sin{t}, \\qquad y'(t)=\\cos{t}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{\\cos t}{-\\sin t} = -\\cot t\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082972 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bda136-40a9-576a-b85c-4d4ebefaeb27" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parametric Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/id #uuid "148e5378-9177-59ba-9b1e-3633c940babd" :question/math-academy-id "e-596" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n$x=te^t, \\quad y=e^{-t}, \\qquad -\\infty < t <\\infty$,\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=1$." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y$, we get\n\n$$\nx'(t) = e^t + te^t = (1+t)e^t, \\qquad y'(t)=-e^{-t}\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\frac{\\mathrm{d} y}{\\mathrm{d} x} & = \\frac{- {e}^{- t}}{( 1 + t ) {e}^{t}} \\\\  & = - \\frac{1}{( 1 + t ) {e}^{2 t}} .\\end{array}$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=1$, the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}{\\frac{\\mathrm{d} y}{\\mathrm{d} x} |}_{t = 1} & = - \\frac{1}{{e}^{2 ( 1 )} ( 1 + 1 )} \\\\  & = - \\frac{1}{2 {e}^{2}} .\\end{array}$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083522 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0bda136-40a9-576a-b85c-4d4ebefaeb27" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parametric Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5ec03d0-7322-5f58-b3ae-7b1eb9ccc6d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8e^{5}}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080631} {:answer/id #uuid "f9cb97db-187f-5526-931e-cbc2f5e02dea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5e^{4}}{\\sqrt{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080632} {:answer/id #uuid "03709d50-0fa9-5eb1-be2a-12bd75719399" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{3}}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080633} {:answer/id #uuid "704dc8a6-7814-52e4-88a8-c81f04287f3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4e^{5}}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080634} {:answer/id #uuid "7da078bf-46dd-5f1d-b83f-becf7a45d04e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8e^{5}}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5ec03d0-7322-5f58-b3ae-7b1eb9ccc6d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8e^{5}}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080631} :answer-field/id #uuid "037556c8-fd10-5e4a-b6e0-378e32bb8f71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186080630}] :question/id #uuid "f252b1a9-57b3-57ad-97f5-a61e75b56356" :question/math-academy-id "q-20991" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$x = \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}, y = \\frac{e^{t}}{2t}, - \\infty  < t < \\infty $,\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t = 5$."}]}
